.*
.* WRKJOBQ: every job queue, or the jobs waiting on one. The columns
.* sit where the V7R1M0 captures have them
.* (golden/verified/oracle71/panels); a queue's status comes one
.* column in from its heading, as the driver gives it.
:PNLGRP.
:CLASS NAME=OPTCL BASETYPE=ACTION.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NAMECL BASETYPE='CHAR 10'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NBRCL BASETYPE='CHAR 6'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=STSCL BASETYPE='CHAR 8'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=CNTCL BASETYPE='ZONED 4 0'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=PTYCL BASETYPE='ZONED 1 0'.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=OPT CLASS=OPTCL.
:VAR NAME=QUEUE CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=LIB CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=JOBS CLASS=CNTCL.
:VAR NAME=SBS CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=STATUS CLASS=STSCL.
:VAR NAME=QSTS CLASS=STSCL.
:VAR NAME=JOB CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=USER CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=NUMBER CLASS=NBRCL.
:VAR NAME=PTY CLASS=PTYCL.
:VAR NAME=JSTS CLASS=STSCL.
:LISTDEF NAME=QUEUES VARS='OPT QUEUE LIB JOBS SBS STATUS'.
:LISTDEF NAME=JOBS VARS='OPT JOB USER NUMBER PTY JSTS'.
:KEYL HELP='KEYS/JQKEYS' NAME=JQKEYS.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEUP ACTION=PAGEUP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEDOWN ACTION=PAGEDOWN.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F4 ACTION='RETURN 4'.F4=Prompt
:KEYI KEY=F5 ACTION='RETURN 5'.F5=Refresh
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:KEYI KEY=F24 ACTION=MOREKEYS.F24=More keys
:KEYI KEY=F9 ACTION=RETRIEVE.F9=Retrieve
:EKEYL.
:KEYL HELP='KEYS/JOBKEYS' NAME=JOBKEYS.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEUP ACTION=PAGEUP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEDOWN ACTION=PAGEDOWN.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F4 ACTION='RETURN 4'.F4=Prompt
:KEYI KEY=F6 ACTION='CMD ?SBMJOB'.F6=Submit job
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:KEYI KEY=F21 ACTION='CMD WRKSBS'.F21=Subsystem
:KEYI KEY=F22 ACTION='CMD WRKJOBSCDE'.F22=Work with job schedule entries
:KEYI KEY=F24 ACTION=MOREKEYS.F24=More keys
:KEYI KEY=F5 ACTION='RETURN 5'.F5=Refresh
:KEYI KEY=F9 ACTION=RETRIEVE.F9=Retrieve
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=QUEUES KEYL=JQKEYS HELP=WRKJOBQ ENTER='RETURN 1' TOPSEP=SPACE.Work with All Job Queues
:TOPINST.Type options, press Enter.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=QUEUES.(No job queues)
:LISTACT HELP='QUEUES/OPTIONS' OPTION=2 ENTER='CMD ?CHGJOBQ JOBQ(&LIB./&QUEUE.)'.2=Change
:LISTACT HELP='QUEUES/OPTIONS' OPTION=3 ENTER='CMD HLDJOBQ JOBQ(&LIB./&QUEUE.)'.3=Hold
:LISTACT HELP='QUEUES/OPTIONS' OPTION=4 ENTER='CMD ?DLTJOBQ JOBQ(&LIB./&QUEUE.)'.4=Delete
:LISTACT HELP='QUEUES/OPTIONS' OPTION=5 ENTER='CMD WRKJOBQ JOBQ(&LIB./&QUEUE.)'.5=Work with
:LISTACT HELP='QUEUES/OPTIONS' OPTION=6 ENTER='CMD RLSJOBQ JOBQ(&LIB./&QUEUE.)'.6=Release
:LISTACT HELP='QUEUES/OPTIONS' OPTION=8 ENTER='CMD WRKJOBSCDE'.8=Work with job schedule entries
:LISTACT HELP='QUEUES/OPTIONS' OPTION=9 ENTER='CMD WRKJOBQD JOBQ(&LIB./&QUEUE.)'.9=Description
:LISTACT HELP='QUEUES/OPTIONS' OPTION=14 ENTER='CMD CLRJOBQ JOBQ(&LIB./&QUEUE.)'.14=Clear
:LISTCOL HELP='QUEUES/OPT' VAR=OPT USAGE=INPUT.Opt
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/QUEUE' VAR=QUEUE USAGE=OUTPUT ATCOL=10.Queue
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/LIB' VAR=LIB USAGE=OUTPUT ATCOL=25.Library
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/JOBS' VAR=JOBS USAGE=OUTPUT ATCOL=43.Jobs
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/SBS' VAR=SBS USAGE=OUTPUT ATCOL=53.Subsystem
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/STATUS' VAR=STATUS USAGE=OUTPUT ATCOL=68.Status
:ELIST.
:CMDLINE SIZE=SHORT.Command
:EPANEL.
:PANEL NAME=JOBS KEYL=JOBKEYS HELP=WRKJOBQ ENTER='RETURN 1' TOPSEP=SPACE.Work with Job Queue
:DATA DEPTH=2 COMPACT.
:DATAI HELP='FLD/QUEUE' VAR=QUEUE USAGE=OUTPUT.Queue
:DATAIX VAR=LIB USAGE=OUTPUT.
:DATAIXT.Library
:DATAIX VAR=QSTS USAGE=OUTPUT.
:DATAIXT.Status
:EDATA.
:TOPINST.Type options, press Enter.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=JOBS.(No jobs in job queue)
:LISTACT HELP='JOBS/OPTIONS' OPTION=2 ENTER='CMD ?CHGJOB JOB(&NUMBER./&USER./&JOB.)'.2=Change
:LISTACT HELP='JOBS/OPTIONS' OPTION=3 ENTER='CMD HLDJOB JOB(&NUMBER./&USER./&JOB.)'.3=Hold
:LISTACT HELP='JOBS/OPTIONS' OPTION=4 ENTER='CMD ?ENDJOB JOB(&NUMBER./&USER./&JOB.)'.4=End
:LISTACT HELP='JOBS/OPTIONS' OPTION=5 ENTER='CMD WRKJOB JOB(&NUMBER./&USER./&JOB.)'.5=Work with
:LISTACT HELP='JOBS/OPTIONS' OPTION=6 ENTER='CMD RLSJOB JOB(&NUMBER./&USER./&JOB.)'.6=Release
:LISTCOL HELP='JOBS/OPT' VAR=OPT USAGE=INPUT.Opt
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/JOB' VAR=JOB USAGE=OUTPUT ATCOL=10.Job
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/USER' VAR=USER USAGE=OUTPUT ATCOL=25.User
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/NUMBER' VAR=NUMBER USAGE=OUTPUT ATCOL=40.Number
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/PTY' VAR=PTY USAGE=OUTPUT ATCOL=51.Priority
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/JSTS' VAR=JSTS USAGE=OUTPUT ATCOL=64.Status
:ELIST.
:CMDLINE SIZE=SHORT.Parameters for options 2, 3 or command
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=WRKJOBQ.Work with Job Queues - Help
:P.Job queues with the jobs waiting on them and the subsystem that
takes them; option 5 shows a queue's jobs.
:EHELP.
.* Item, key and option help.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/JQKEYS'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display and returns to where it was started from.
:PT.F4=Prompt
:PD.Prompts the command on the command line, or the command of the
option typed.
:PT.F5=Refresh
:PD.Shows the display again with the current information.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display without acting on what was typed.
:PT.F24=More keys
:PD.Shows the other function keys of the display.
:PT.F9=Retrieve
:PD.Puts the last command run back on the command line; press it again
for the one before.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QUEUES/OPT'.Option
:P.Type the number of an option next to an entry and press Enter. The
options the list allows are shown above it; F1 on one of them explains
it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/QUEUE'.Queue
:P.The queue of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/LIB'.Library
:P.The library of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/JOBS'.Jobs
:P.The job, by name, user and number. A job name alone is enough when
only one job has it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/SBS'.Subsystem
:P.The subsystem of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/STATUS'.Status
:P.The status of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QUEUES/OPTIONS'.Options
:P.Type an option number next to one or more entries and press Enter.
The option runs for each entry it is typed next to, in order.
:PARML.
:PT.2=Change
:PD.Type 2 next to an entry and press Enter to change it. The Change Job
Queue (CHGJOBQ) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.3=Hold
:PD.Type 3 next to an entry and press Enter to hold it. The Hold Job
Queue (HLDJOBQ) command runs for the entry.
:PT.4=Delete
:PD.Type 4 next to an entry and press Enter to delete it. The Delete Job
Queue (DLTJOBQ) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.5=Work with
:PD.Type 5 next to an entry and press Enter to work with it. The Work
with Job Queue (WRKJOBQ) command runs for the entry.
:PT.6=Release
:PD.Type 6 next to an entry and press Enter to release it. The Release
Job Queue (RLSJOBQ) command runs for the entry.
:PT.8=Work with job schedule entries
:PD.Type 8 next to an entry and press Enter to work with job schedule
entries it. The Work with Job Schedule Entries (WRKJOBSCDE) command runs
for the entry.
:PT.9=Description
:PD.Type 9 next to an entry and press Enter to description it.
:PT.14=Clear
:PD.Type 14 next to an entry and press Enter to clear it. The Clear Job
Queue (CLRJOBQ) command runs for the entry.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/JOBKEYS'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display and returns to where it was started from.
:PT.F4=Prompt
:PD.Prompts the command on the command line, or the command of the
option typed.
:PT.F6=Submit job
:PD.Runs SBMJOB.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display without acting on what was typed.
:PT.F21=Subsystem
:PD.Runs WRKSBS.
:PT.F22=Work with job schedule entries
:PD.Runs WRKJOBSCDE.
:PT.F24=More keys
:PD.Shows the other function keys of the display.
:PT.F5=Refresh
:PD.Shows the display again with the current information.
:PT.F9=Retrieve
:PD.Puts the last command run back on the command line; press it again
for the one before.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='JOBS/OPT'.Option
:P.Type the number of an option next to an entry and press Enter. The
options the list allows are shown above it; F1 on one of them explains
it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/JOB'.Job
:P.The job, by name, user and number. A job name alone is enough when
only one job has it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/USER'.User
:P.The user of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/NUMBER'.Number
:P.The number of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/PTY'.Priority
:P.The priority of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/JSTS'.Status
:P.The status of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='JOBS/OPTIONS'.Options
:P.Type an option number next to one or more entries and press Enter.
The option runs for each entry it is typed next to, in order.
:PARML.
:PT.2=Change
:PD.Type 2 next to an entry and press Enter to change it. The Change Job
(CHGJOB) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.3=Hold
:PD.Type 3 next to an entry and press Enter to hold it. The Hold Job
(HLDJOB) command runs for the entry.
:PT.4=End
:PD.Type 4 next to an entry and press Enter to end it. The End Job
(ENDJOB) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.5=Work with
:PD.Type 5 next to an entry and press Enter to work with it. The Work
with Job (WRKJOB) command runs for the entry.
:PT.6=Release
:PD.Type 6 next to an entry and press Enter to release it. The Release
Job (RLSJOB) command runs for the entry.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
